  "conclusion": "1) Fixing the Pyro simulate() conditioning bug drops unconnected neuron 2 from 0.1427 to ~0, revealing that the original single-pulse probe only produced 0.0079 downstream dF/F0 (SNR < 0.8). 2) In an informative high-SNR multi-pulse regime (neuron 1 peak = 0.159 dF/F0, R^2 = 0.972), freeing all parameters shows strong compensation across g_max, neuron1 G, kinetics, and gcamp.gain. 3) Pinning the GCaMP scale gauge lifts heldout R^2 to 0.996 and recovers k_off within 11% and total Ca2+ timescale within CI90 (27.1s vs 29.2s), yet g_max (0.0163 vs 0.050) still trades off against postsynaptic leak conductance G (0.321 vs 0.50) and v_th_ca \u2014 proving voltage-free Ca2+ imaging identifies predictive trajectories and dimensionless ratios, not isolated single-edge nS conductances."
